-- הסכם אופק חדש (25.12.2008) — העותק החתום והרשום, עם טבלאות הנספחים: a
-- second copy of the base agreement of 25.12.2008 — the scan of the copy
-- signed on 25 December 2008 and registered in 2009, which the corpus
-- publishes beside the born-digital text the base agreement is encoded from
-- (`base-agreement-<n>`, l4/agreements/ofek-hadash/2008-12-25_ofek-hadash_base-agreement/,
-- "the primary"). Its words are the primary's, row for row, except:
--   - the front: a registration stamp and hand-written marks, and the day and
--     month of signing written in by hand, which the primary leaves blank;
--   - five cross-references: §§109(ב), 110 and 111, in the chapter on
--     non-academic first deputies, cite the principals' sections 71(ג), 72
--     and 67, where the primary cites the first deputies' 98(ג), 99 and 93
--     (F-ofek-hadash-base-registry-copy-a); §120(ב) cites §117 where the
--     primary cites §118 (-b); §147(ג) cites "146(א) (1)" where the primary
--     cites "147(א) (1)" (-c);
--   - two numbers printed twice ("4949" in §100, "104104" in §107), which the
--     corpus marks [כך במקור];
--   - page 50, which the scan lacks: §122 breaks off, and §§123–126 are not
--     in this copy (the primary has them);
--   - the printing: bullets and letters before the lines of the worked
--     examples, sums written the other way round, the formula lines of §§55,
--     79 and 108 set (by the corpus) as the headings of the next section, and
--     four tables (§§44(ג), 66(ז), 66(י), 138(א)(1)) printed as tables where
--     the primary's text runs their cells one to a line;
--   - the annexes: the work-week tables of annex א' (a primary school) and
--     annex ב' (a junior high school), each for three ages, and a junior-high
--     table for positions below a third, which the primary does not publish
--     and takes as named inputs (§27(ז)–(יא), §131(ג)).
-- So every row the two copies share is cited "as in the primary", by the
-- module and the rule that encode it there. What this file encodes is what
-- differs: the day of signing; the five cross-references as this copy prints
-- them, each read as the primary reads it, with the difference asserted; and
-- the annexes, as data, cell for cell as the corpus publishes them, with the
-- checks the agreement's own rules make of them (§§15, 17, 24, 26, 27, 131).
-- The tables feed the primary's named inputs; the primary is not edited.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT `base-agreement-common`
IMPORT `base-agreement-15`
IMPORT `base-agreement-17`
IMPORT `base-agreement-24`
IMPORT `base-agreement-26`
IMPORT `base-agreement-27`
IMPORT `base-agreement-81`
IMPORT `base-agreement-82`
IMPORT `base-agreement-110`
IMPORT `base-agreement-111`
IMPORT `base-agreement-117`
IMPORT `base-agreement-120`
IMPORT `base-agreement-131`
IMPORT `base-agreement-146`

§ `הסכם אופק חדש — 25.12.2008 (העותק החתום והרשום, עם טבלאות הנספחים)`

