-- att_3: a junior-high table for low positions. It prints no age and no
-- one-school row for a mother; its positions are shares of the 36-hour
-- week (9 hours = 25%), the week of a teacher under 50, as the checks
-- below confirm.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1/p1 akn:att_3__hc_1/t1
`the junior-high table for positions below a third` MEANS
    `annexed week table` WITH
        `annexed table's title`   IS "טבלת שבוע עבודה בחטיבת ביניים להיקפי משרה נמוכים ברפורמה *"
        `annexed table's stage`   IS `a junior high school`
        `annexed table's age`     IS `up to age 50`
        `annexed table's columns` IS LIST
            `an annexed column` (25.00%) 6 1 2 9 NOTHING (JUST 1.5),
            `an annexed column` (22.22%) 5 1 2 8 NOTHING (JUST 1.5),
            `an annexed column` (19.44%) 4 1 2 7 NOTHING (JUST 1.5)

§§ `הנספחים — מה הטבלאות קובעות, והבדיקות`

GIVEN c IS AN `annexed week column`
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the annexed column's week` c IS
    `a week of` (c's `annexed frontal hours`) (c's `annexed individual hours`) (c's `annexed stay hours`)

-- §27(ז) (`the hours annexes א and ב give`) and §27(ח) (`the hours annexes
-- ג and ג1 give`): the week of a position is the column printed for it.
-- A position the table does not print has no week here (convention
-- thresholds.missing-row).
GIVEN t IS AN `annexed week table`, position IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `work week`
DECIDE `the week annexed for the position` t position IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `annexed position` EQUALS position) (t's `annexed table's columns`)
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (`the annexed column's week` c)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING

-- The table for a teacher's age (§26, §27(יא)): up to 50 the first; from 50
-- the second; from 55 the third, but not for a new teacher (the heading's
-- "לא חל על מורים חדשים- החל מתשס"ח"), who stays on the second — §26(ג)'s
-- two hours off from 50 and no more.
GIVEN `an existing teacher` IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `annexed table's ages`
DECIDE `the annexed table for the age` `an existing teacher` age IS
    BRANCH IF age AT LEAST 55 AND `an existing teacher` THEN `from age 55`
           IF age AT LEAST 50                           THEN `from age 50`
           OTHERWISE                                         `up to age 50`

-- The full position a table's positions are shares of: §15's week in a
-- primary school, §17's in a junior high school, less §26's age hours for
-- an existing teacher in a full position.
GIVEN t IS AN `annexed week table`
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the full week of the annexed table` t IS
    `a week of` (full's `frontal hours` MINUS off's `frontal hours off`) (full's `individual hours` MINUS off's `individual hours off`) (full's `stay hours`)
    WHERE
        full MEANS IF t's `annexed table's stage` EQUALS `a primary school`
                   THEN `a primary teacher's full week`
                   ELSE `a junior-high teacher's full week`
        age MEANS CONSIDER t's `annexed table's age`
                  WHEN `up to age 50` THEN 49
                  WHEN `from age 50` THEN 50
                  WHEN `from age 55` THEN 55
        off MEANS `the age hours` TRUE TRUE age

-- *, ** and the example under them: a mother's stay hours are the table's
-- "שעות שהייה למורה אם" — in one school, from 79% of a position ("79% משרה
-- ומעלה"), and in several schools, by her position in all of them, if it is
-- 79% or more, even where her position in the reform school is below 79%.
-- In a school where she works off the reform, the rules there go on, by her
-- position in that school: no rule of this agreement. The reduction changes
-- neither her position base nor her position (*): only her stay hours.
-- A position printed twice with two answers (annex ב', from 50 and from
-- 55) takes the smaller, the reading F-ofek-hadash-base-registry-copy-e
-- adopts (convention reading.consistent).
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p5 akn:att_1__hc_1/p6 akn:att_2__hc_1/p5 akn:att_2__hc_1/p6 akn:att_3__hc_1/p3 akn:att_3__hc_1/p4
GIVEN `in several schools` IS A BOOLEAN, c IS AN `annexed week column`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the mother's cell of the column` `in several schools` c IS
    IF `in several schools`
    THEN c's `annexed mother's stay hours in several schools`
    ELSE c's `annexed mother's stay hours in one school`

GIVEN t IS AN `annexed week table`
      position IS A NUMBER
      `position in all schools` IS A NUMBER
      `in several schools` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `work week`
DECIDE `a mother's week annexed for the position` t position `position in all schools` `in several schools` IS
    CONSIDER cells
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF `position in all schools` AT LEAST (79%)
        THEN CONSIDER `the mother's cells`
             WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST (`the annexed column's week` c)
             WHEN m FOLLOWED BY more THEN JUST (`a week of` (c's `annexed frontal hours`) (c's `annexed individual hours`) (minimum (m FOLLOWED BY more)))
        ELSE JUST (`the annexed column's week` c)
    WHERE
        cells MEANS filter (GIVEN x YIELD x's `annexed position` EQUALS position) (t's `annexed table's columns`)
        `the mother's cells` MEANS catMaybes (map (GIVEN x YIELD `the mother's cell of the column` `in several schools` x) cells)

-- A mother's stay hours never exceed the stay hours of her column.
GIVEN c IS AN `annexed week column`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a mother's stay hours are within the column's` c IF
        all (GIVEN m YIELD m AT MOST c's `annexed stay hours`) (catMaybes (LIST c's `annexed mother's stay hours in one school`, c's `annexed mother's stay hours in several schools`))

-- The checks the agreement's own rules make of a table.
GIVEN c IS AN `annexed week column`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annexed column adds up` c IF
    `hours of the week` (`the annexed column's week` c) EQUALS c's `annexed weekly hours`

-- §27(ז): the hours of a part-time position are in proportion to the full
-- position's; the printed position is the column's hours over the full
-- week's, to the hundredth of a percent the table prints.
GIVEN t IS AN `annexed week table`, c IS AN `annexed week column`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annexed position is the hours' share` t c IF
    `to the agora` (100 TIMES c's `annexed weekly hours` DIVIDED BY `hours of the week` (`the full week of the annexed table` t)) EQUALS 100 TIMES c's `annexed position`

-- The one-school row is printed from 79% of a position, and only there.
GIVEN c IS AN `annexed week column`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the one-school cell is printed from 79%` c IF
    isJust (c's `annexed mother's stay hours in one school`) EQUALS (c's `annexed position` AT LEAST (79%))

GIVEN t IS AN `annexed week table`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annexed table checks` t IF
        all `the annexed column adds up` (t's `annexed table's columns`)
    AND all (GIVEN c YIELD `the annexed position is the hours' share` t c) (t's `annexed table's columns`)
    AND all `a mother's stay hours are within the column's` (t's `annexed table's columns`)

`the annexed week tables` MEANS LIST
    `annex א up to age 50`, `annex א from age 50`, `annex א from age 55`,
    `annex ב up to age 50`, `annex ב from age 50`, `annex ב from age 55`,
    `the junior-high table for positions below a third`

`the full-position tables` MEANS LIST
    `annex א up to age 50`, `annex א from age 50`, `annex א from age 55`,
    `annex ב up to age 50`, `annex ב from age 50`, `annex ב from age 55`

#ASSERT all `the annexed table checks` `the annexed week tables`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD all `the one-school cell is printed from 79%` (t's `annexed table's columns`)) `the full-position tables`

-- §§15, 17 and 26: the full position of each table is §15's or §17's week
-- less the age hours §26 gives at that age.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD `the week annexed for the position` t 1 EQUALS JUST (`the full week of the annexed table` t)) `the full-position tables`
#ASSERT `the full week of the annexed table` `annex א up to age 50` EQUALS `a primary teacher's full week`
#ASSERT `the full week of the annexed table` `annex ב up to age 50` EQUALS `a junior-high teacher's full week`
#ASSERT `the week annexed for the position` `annex א from age 55` 1 EQUALS JUST (`a week of` 23 4 5)
#ASSERT `the week annexed for the position` `annex ב from age 50` 1 EQUALS JUST (`a week of` 21 4 9)
-- The choice of table agrees with §26 over every age from 30 to 70.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN a YIELD `the annexed table for the age` FALSE a EQUALS (IF a AT LEAST 50 THEN `from age 50` ELSE `up to age 50`)) (range 30 70)
#ASSERT `the annexed table for the age` TRUE 55 EQUALS `from age 55`

-- §24: in a full position a mother's stay hours fall by 2.5, in every
-- table and in one school or several.
GIVEN t IS AN `annexed week table`
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `a mother's full week by §24 on the annexed table` t IS
    `a week of` (w's `frontal hours`) (w's `individual hours`) (w's `stay hours` MINUS `a mother's stay-hours reduction in a full position`)
    WHERE
        w MEANS `the full week of the annexed table` t

#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD `a mother's week annexed for the position` t 1 1 FALSE EQUALS JUST (`a mother's full week by §24 on the annexed table` t)) `the full-position tables`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD `a mother's week annexed for the position` t 1 1 TRUE EQUALS JUST (`a mother's full week by §24 on the annexed table` t)) `the full-position tables`

-- §27(ז): a half position by the table is half the full week in hours.
#ASSERT `the part-time weekly hours in proportion` `a primary teacher's full week` (50.00%) EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `the week annexed for the position` `annex א up to age 50` (50.00%) EQUALS JUST (`a week of` 13 2 3)

-- The example under the tables: a mother in 50% of a position in one reform
-- school and 40% in another off the reform (90% in all) has 1.5 stay hours
-- in a primary school (annex א') and 3 in a junior high school (annex ב').
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p7 akn:att_1__hc_1/p8 akn:att_2__hc_1/p7 akn:att_2__hc_1/p8
`the example's mother's positions` MEANS LIST (50%), (40%)
#ASSERT `a mother's week annexed for the position` `annex א up to age 50` (50.00%) (90%) TRUE EQUALS JUST (`a week of` 13 2 1.5)
#ASSERT `a mother's week annexed for the position` `annex ב up to age 50` (50.00%) (90%) TRUE EQUALS JUST (`a week of` 12 2 3)
-- In all below 79%, no reduction; in one school, the one-school row.
#ASSERT `a mother's week annexed for the position` `annex א up to age 50` (50.00%) (70%) TRUE EQUALS JUST (`a week of` 13 2 3)
#ASSERT `a mother's week annexed for the position` `annex א up to age 50` (80.56%) (80.56%) FALSE EQUALS JUST (`a week of` 21 4 2)

-- att_3's *: the table is for a teacher in one school of several, in a
-- subject the teaching personnel division approved for low positions, and
-- for paramedical teachers, whose position in the reform in all is "גבוה מ
-- 33.3%" (convention thresholds.above). §27(ח) says "not below a third":
-- at the positions whole hours make (h/36), the two agree.
@ref akn:att_3__hc_1/p2
GIVEN `teaches an approved subject in several schools` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a paramedical teacher` IS A BOOLEAN
      `position in the reform in all` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the junior-high table for low positions applies` `teaches an approved subject in several schools` `a paramedical teacher` `position in the reform in all` IF
        (`teaches an approved subject in several schools` OR `a paramedical teacher`)
    AND `position in the reform in all` GREATER THAN (33.3%)

#ASSERT all (GIVEN h YIELD (h DIVIDED BY 36 GREATER THAN (33.3%)) EQUALS (h DIVIDED BY 36 AT LEAST 1/3)) (range 1 36)
#ASSERT `the junior-high table for low positions applies` TRUE FALSE (12 DIVIDED BY 36)
#ASSERT `the week annexed for the position` `the junior-high table for positions below a third` (25.00%) EQUALS JUST (`a week of` 6 1 2)

-- F-ofek-hadash-base-registry-copy-d: §131(ג)'s example takes 24 frontal
-- hours as "היקף משרה 93%" by annex א'; annex א' prints that column at
-- 94.44%, with Z = 34 hours in all, which is the example's Z. The table
-- governs (convention precedence.table); nothing in the example's sum turns
-- on the 93%.
`annex א's column of 24 frontal hours` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `annexed frontal hours` EQUALS 24) (`annex א up to age 50`'s `annexed table's columns`)

#ASSERT (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `annexed weekly hours`) `annex א's column of 24 frontal hours`) EQUALS LIST (`the example's counsellor`'s Z)

`annex א prints 24 frontal hours at another position than §131's example` MEANS
        (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `annexed position`) `annex א's column of 24 frontal hours`) EQUALS LIST (94.44%)
    AND NOT (94.44% EQUALS `the position §131's example names for 24 frontal hours`)
#ASSERT `annex א prints 24 frontal hours at another position than §131's example`

-- F-ofek-hadash-base-registry-copy-e: annex ב' from 50 prints 73.53% twice,
-- and from 55 prints 75.00% twice, each time with the same hours and with
-- a mother's stay hours in several schools of 5 in the first column and 4
-- in the second. Read as 4 (convention reading.consistent: the 2 hours off
-- the 6 stay hours the columns beside it give).
GIVEN t IS AN `annexed week table`, position IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `annexed week column`
DECIDE `the columns printed for` t position IS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `annexed position` EQUALS position) (t's `annexed table's columns`)

GIVEN t IS AN `annexed week table`, position IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a position printed twice with two mother's cells` t position IF
    CONSIDER `the columns printed for` t position
    WHEN a FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER rest
        WHEN b FOLLOWED BY more THEN
                null more
            AND `the annexed column's week` a EQUALS `the annexed column's week` b
            AND NOT (a's `annexed mother's stay hours in several schools` EQUALS b's `annexed mother's stay hours in several schools`)
        WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE

`annex ב prints one position twice with two mother's cells` MEANS
        `a position printed twice with two mother's cells` `annex ב from age 50` (73.53%)
    AND `a position printed twice with two mother's cells` `annex ב from age 55` (75.00%)
